  "content": {
    "id": "p29-q12",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "From the origin at a window, a ball has $x=24t$ and $y=-5t^2+10t$.\nIt lands on the ground 4 m below the window.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p29-q12-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Find the time of flight (exact).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\left(1+\\dfrac{3\\sqrt5}{5}\\right)\\text{ s}$",
          "worked": "At the ground, $y=-4$.\n$$\\begin{aligned}-5t^2+10t&=-4\\\\5t^2-10t-4&=0\\\\t&=\\frac{10\\pm\\sqrt{180}}{10}\\\\t&=1+\\frac{3\\sqrt5}{5}\\text{ s}.\\end{aligned}$$\nThe negative root is rejected because $t>0$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q12-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Find how far from the base it lands to 1 d.p.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$56.2\\text{ m}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}x&=24t\\\\x&=24\\left(1+\\frac{3\\sqrt5}{5}\\right)\\\\x&\\approx56.2\\text{ m}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p29-q12-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Find the impact speed (exact).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$6\\sqrt{21}\\text{ m/s}$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\dot{x}&=24,\\qquad\\dot{y}=10-10t.\\end{aligned}$$\nAt impact, $5t^2-10t=4$, so\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\dot{y}^{\\,2}&=100(1-t)^2\\\\\\dot{y}^{\\,2}&=100(t^2-2t+1)\\\\\\dot{y}^{\\,2}&=100\\left(\\frac45+1\\right)\\\\\\dot{y}^{\\,2}&=180.\\end{aligned}$$\nHence the impact speed is\n$$\\begin{aligned}V&=\\sqrt{\\dot{x}^{\\,2}+\\dot{y}^{\\,2}}\\\\V&=\\sqrt{576+180}\\\\V&=6\\sqrt{21}\\text{ m/s}.\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      }
    ]
  },
